    <string name="size_cap_hint">The range is derived from your screen and bounded by two hard limits. The smallest step is 18mm, below which a dog can no longer make out the shape — canine acuity is about 20/75, and a dog watching a phone on the floor is 30–60cm away. The largest step is 45% of your screen\'s short edge, because prey that fills the field has nowhere to run, and running is what triggers the chase. A phone simply cannot fit paw-sized prey and room to run at the same time, so playability wins; a tablet has room for both and the range widens automatically.</string>
